cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EcoMine Observatory, please cite it as below. This is an early
  (v0.1.0) research tool. As of this release it has one supervised-classifier
  accuracy figure, from a single site (Kangala, South Africa); that figure has
  not been shown to transfer to other sites. Cite it as early-stage software,
  not as a validated detector.
title: "EcoMine Observatory"
abstract: >-
  Open-source multi-sensor screening tools for the environmental footprint of
  mining in the Middle East and Africa, built on Google Earth Engine and the
  opengeos stack. Produces spectral indices, change indicators with
  site-adaptive thresholds, and machine-readable provenance. Emits screening
  signals for expert review, not detections, attributions or compliance
  findings.
type: software
